        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T02:31:20Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools): a plasma torch row carries a cut-data recipe by material and thickness\n\nSlice 1 of #1521, tool side. A torch cutting row may state a plasma\nrecipe (CuttingRow::plasma, tools::plasma_cut::PlasmaCutData): plate\nthickness, kerf, and optional cut height, pierce height, pierce delay,\ntransfer height, puddle jump, amperage, arc voltage, pierce capacity and\nan edge-start mark. A blank value means the controller's own table.\n\nThe tool door refuses a bad recipe by name: a non-torch tool, a bad\nnumber, a puddle jump without a pierce height, a material and thickness\ntwice, and a plate thicker than the pierce capacity without an edge\nstart. A recipe is picked only by material and exact thickness\n(plasma_row_for); selection by material alone never takes one.\n\nThe project file and the tool library write the recipe under the row's\nadditive `plasma` key. The tool editor keeps a recipe in the draft and\ndoes not draw it as a material row. No toolpath or posted output changes.\n\nRefs #1521\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
